"""Render the audit evidence as a standalone review report, outside the public site."""
import json, pathlib, html
root=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'reports/seo/internal-linking'
load=lambda name:json.loads((root/name).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
before=load('live-before.json'); after=load('built-acceptance.json')
esc=lambda value:html.escape(str(value))
table=lambda heads,rows:'<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+esc(h)+'</th>' for h in heads)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(c)+'</td>' for c in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table>'
rows=[]
for a,b in zip(before['components'],after['components']):rows.append([a['criterion'],a['weight'],a['defects'],b['defects'],f"{b['earned']:.2f}"])
counts=lambda d:[len(d[k]) for k in ['broken','missingFragments','noncanonical','orphans','unreachable','deep','noBody']]
findings=list(zip(['Broken public page destinations','Missing fragment targets','Anchors using legacy destinations','Orphan public pages','Public pages unreachable from homepage','Pages deeper than three clicks','Pages without content inbound links'],counts(before),counts(after)))
browser=load('browser-acceptance.json')
content=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Peninsula Insider internal-linking discovery and acceptance</title>
<style>body{{font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#14202a;background:#f2efea;margin:0}}main{{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:40px 24px}}h1,h2{{line-height:1.2}}h1{{font-size:38px}}.scores{{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap}}.score{{background:white;padding:24px;flex:1;min-width:230px;border-top:5px solid #10527e}}strong.number{{font-size:42px;display:block}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background:white;margin:20px 0;font-size:15px}}th,td{{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #d9d6d0}}a{{color:#10527e}}code{{font-size:14px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}}.note{{border-left:4px solid #10527e;padding:12px 20px;background:white}}@media(max-width:600px){{h1{{font-size:29px}}table{{font-size:12px}}th,td{{padding:6px}}}}</style><main>
<p>11 October 2026 · Source SHA f05b40f902a3b6dd7de919ee196afde64066d123</p><h1>Internal linking: full discovery, corrections and acceptance</h1>
<div class="scores"><div class="score">Verified live baseline<strong class="number">{before['score']}/100</strong>{before['pages']} fetched HTML pages; {before['eligible']} public canonical pages assessed.</div><div class="score">Tested local candidate<strong class="number">{after['score']}/100</strong>{after['pages']} built HTML pages; {after['eligible']} public canonical pages assessed.</div></div>
<p class="note">The candidate is local and has not been deployed. This is a project internal-linking acceptance score, not a Google score, an overall SEO grade or a guarantee of indexing, rankings or traffic. The newly useful weekend archive index adds one public canonical page to the candidate.</p>
<h2>Discovery and grading method</h2><p>Discovery combined the live XML sitemap, a recursive same-origin HTML crawl and public pages found in a clean build of the deployed source. 701 live URLs were requested, with 700 returning HTML. The one 404 was Cloudflare's email-protection helper, which is infrastructure rather than a public editorial destination. Two initial transient request failures returned 200 on recheck.</p>
<p>The DOM audit follows actual HTML anchor hrefs, resolves relative URLs, retains fragments and query parameters, classifies navigation versus content links, checks canonical destinations and fragment IDs, calculates inbound links, and uses breadth-first search from the homepage. Noindex pages, redirect documents and private/machine utility namespaces are reported in the inventory but are outside the public-canonical score. The agent reader boundary is preserved.</p>
<p>Each criterion earns its weight multiplied by the fraction without defects. Canonical and reachability criteria use affected pages rather than raw link counts so repeated sitewide navigation cannot dilute those defects. A passing build additionally requires zero broken routes, missing fragments, legacy destinations, orphans and unreachable public pages. Three clicks is a project usability target, not a Google requirement. Contextual relevance is reviewed through source rules and regression fixtures rather than assigned a fabricated semantic percentage.</p>
{table(['Criterion','Weight','Live defects','Candidate defects','Candidate points'],rows)}
<h2>Observed defects and corrections</h2>{table(['Finding','Live','Candidate'],findings)}
<ul><li>Restored every published Insider Picks edition to its separate archive. The previous twelve-edition cap orphaned older selections.</li><li>Turned the empty weekend archive landing page into a dated, crawlable archive using existing shared page styles. Past recommendations are explicitly historical. It is linked from the current weekend page and the site index and included in the sitemap.</li><li>Restored paths into existing public guides, regions, signature events, awards and publication pages. Added a direct, accurately labelled cancellation-notice link without promoting the cancelled festival as an upcoming event.</li><li>Removed the site index's fifty-article cap, preserving older published reading outside the fresh Journal feed.</li><li>Rewired anchor hrefs through the destinations declared by existing redirect/canonical pages. The build step preserves editorial text, scripts, metadata, query parameters and valid fragments. Unknown destinations and invalid fragments are held for a failing audit rather than guessed.</li><li>Related Journal reading now ranks shared topics and recorded places/entities ahead of format. Explicit editorial selections remain first. Unrelated recency filler is omitted from this rail. Navigation and the full archives provide discovery separately.</li></ul>
<h2>Contextual linking assessment</h2><p>The source already has category hubs, venue and place pages, breadcrumbs, related reading and referenced venue/place/experience/itinerary cards. Descriptive venue and story titles provide named links. Decorative duplicate image anchors are supported by a nearby named link to the same destination; image alt text is not filled with invented photographic claims for SEO. Editorial-only formats retain their existing boundaries around venue-card promotion.</p>
<p>The strongest existing topic paths are wine → cellar doors → wineries; Eat &amp; Drink → dining guides → venues; Explore → places and regions → experiences and plans; and What's On → dated editions → event or cancellation details. The corrections restore discoverability and remove avoidable hops within those paths. Shared references are evidence of an editorial relationship, not proof that every possible link should be inserted.</p>
<h2>Validation and release boundary</h2><p>Eight targeted regression tests cover DOM parsing, canonical chains and cycles, query/fragment preservation, local fragment checks versus consent controls, orphan detection, decorative-link handling, topic-based relevance, explicit editorial precedence and idempotent rewiring. Tests were checked with the Node 22 CI runtime. The complete normal build and its existing regression gates were run on the final candidate. Browser acceptance checks desktop and mobile widths, visible headings, overflow, complete archives and representative navigation.</p>
<p>Browser evidence: {len(browser['checks'])} page/viewport checks. Review the <a href="browser-acceptance.json">browser results</a>, <a href="picks-390.png">mobile Picks archive</a> and <a href="weekend-archive-390.png">mobile weekend archive</a>.</p>
<p>Production publication requires release approval. Until publication and another live crawl, the public site retains the baseline grade. After release, verify deployment SHA, re-run discovery and the same audit, then inspect Search Console over subsequent weeks to assess indexing and search performance. Search Console performance was not queried or inferred in this audit.</p>
<h2>Evidence and reproduction</h2><ul><li><a href="live-before.json">Live score and complete defect lists</a></li><li><a href="iteration-1.json">Navigation iteration</a> and <a href="iteration-2.json">Canonical-link iteration</a></li><li><a href="built-acceptance.json">Final candidate acceptance</a></li><li><a href="canonical-rewires.json">Exact anchor rewires</a></li><li><a href="page-inventory.csv">Every built page and its classification</a></li><li><a href="link-inventory.csv.gz">Distinct anchor records (compressed CSV)</a></li></ul>
<p>From the repository root: <code>python ops/scripts/internal-link-discovery.py --source-score ops/reports/seo/internal-linking/live-before.json</code>. From <code>next/</code>: <code>node scripts/internal-link-quality.mjs --dist ../ops/reports/seo/internal-linking/live-html --json ../ops/reports/seo/internal-linking/live-after.json</code>. The regular <code>npm run build</code> runs the rewiring and acceptance gate.</p>
<h2>Best-practice sources</h2><p><a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/links-crawlable">Google Search Central: Link best practices</a> supports crawlable anchors, descriptive text, relevant contextual links and inbound links to important pages. <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/seo-starter-guide">Google's SEO Starter Guide</a> supports logical organization, useful linked resources and realistic measurement of search effects.</p></main></html>'''
(root/'report.html').write_text(content,encoding='utf-8')
print('Report written to',root/'report.html')
